# What the panels promise.
#
# A link inside a turbo-frame replaces the panel rather than the page, and the
# answer has to contain that panel or the browser blanks it — at HTTP 200, with
# nothing in any log and nothing in the console. These are the assertions that
# can see that.

visit /
expect frame results

# The search box drives the panel. That is why typing does not reload the page,
# and it is the one piece of this design a spec should hold still.
expect form search targets frame results

fill q json
submit
expect status 200
expect frame results

within results {
    expect item symbol
}

# A result link leaves the panel behind: it goes to a whole symbol page, which
# is not a panel and cannot be delivered as one, so the link has to say so.
#
# This is the assertion of the fix rather than of the symptom. Somebody who
# removes the `_top` will fail here, on the line that says why it was there.
expect link "json.Json.Null" targets page
